{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.chi_b3_measured_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.chi_b3_measured_pos","kind":"theorem","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L397-L400","doc":"The measured three-body cumulant is positive (AME2020 Ursell inversion,\n`he4_body_order_shortfall_location_probe.py`), which is what\n`complete_b3_neg` contradicts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.complete_b3_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.complete_b3_neg","kind":"theorem","line":392,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L392-L395","doc":"**So the saturating complete-graph branch has a negative three-body\ncumulant** whenever the deuteron binds. `b₂ = L_pn = 2.224566 MeV > 0` gives\n`b₃ = −4.449132 MeV`, against the measured `b₃ = +1.426222 MeV`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.complete_b3_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.complete_b3_eq","kind":"theorem","line":384,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L384-L390","doc":"**Under that cancellation the three-body cumulant is minus twice the\ntwo-body one.** With `L_pp + L_nn = −2·L_pn`, the complete graph gives\n`b₂ = B(²H) = L_pn` and `B̄(3) = (L_pp + L_nn)/2 + 2·L_pn = L_pn`, so the Ursell\ninversion `b₃ = B̄(3) − 3·b₂` returns `−2·L_pn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.complete_A2_coefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.complete_A2_coefficient","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L366-L382","doc":"**The complete-graph branch saturates only under an exact sign\ncancellation.** For the complete graph on `A` sites the typed sum is\n`B = L_pp·C(Z,2) + L_pn·Z·N + L_nn·C(N,2)`; along the isobaric line\n`Z = (A−d)/2`, `N = (A+d)/2` the coefficient of `A²` is\n`(L_pp + L_nn + 2·L_pn)/8`. Written without division, as the doubled form: the\n`A²` coefficient of `8·B` is `L_pp + L_nn + 2·L_pn`.\n\n`QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation.complete_graph_no_saturation` assumes a single\n`ε > 0`, so it does not cover the mixed-sign case; this identity is what shows\nthe case exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.measured_ratio_exceeds_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.measured_ratio_exceeds_bound","kind":"theorem","line":360,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L360-L364","doc":"The measured ratio, for the record: `B(⁴He)/B(²H) = 28.2956624/2.224566`\nexceeds the largest value the regular branch can reach by more than a factor\ntwo. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.typed_transferable_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.typed_transferable_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L347-L358","doc":"**The regular branch is refuted by two nuclei.** Along `N = Z` the collapse\ngives `2·B(A) = k_A · Z · (L_pp + L_nn)`, so with `k₂ = 1` (the only graph on two\nsites carrying a bond),\n\n    B(⁴He)/B(²H) = 2·k₄  ≤  2·(4 − 1) = 6,\n\nby the simple-graph degree bound `k ≤ A − 1`. AME2020 gives `12.7196…`. Stated\nas: no admissible `k₄` reproduces the ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.B2S_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.B2S_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L316-L336","doc":"**The collapse.** Under regularity of degree `k` and the mean condition, the\ntyped bond sum is *linear in the nucleon counts* — a one-body self-energy. The\ngraph survives only through the scalar `k`; which pairs are bonded has been\nerased entirely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.mean_of_siteInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.mean_of_siteInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L294-L314","doc":"**The mean condition is forced.** On a regular graph carrying both a bond and\na non-bond between distinct sites, site invariance forces\n`L_pp + L_nn = 2·L_pn` — the `p`–`n` scalar is the arithmetic mean of the\nlike-pair scalars. Strictly weaker than `L_pp = L_pn = L_nn`, which is what the\n*chain* forces; the chain's extra strength comes from its irregularity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.sub_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.sub_pair","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L274-L292","doc":"The two-proton difference on a **regular** graph: only the adjacency\nindicators survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.regular_of_siteInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.regular_of_siteInvariant","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L260-L272","doc":"**A site-invariant typed bond sum on a graph with two different degrees forces\n`L_pn = L_nn`.** Contrapositive form: with `L_pn ≠ L_nn` the graph is regular. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.sub_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.sub_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L249-L258","doc":"The one-proton difference: only the degrees survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.SiteInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.SiteInvariant","kind":"def","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L239-L243","doc":"**Site invariance** — the physical requirement. A nucleus has no arrangement,\nso its binding may depend only on how *many* protons there are, not on which\nsites carry them. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.B2S_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.B2S_eq","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L197-L237","doc":"**Master identity — the typed bond sum in degree / induced-edge\ncoordinates.** Everything below is a corollary of this plus a choice of `S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.sum_ind_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.sum_ind_mem","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L180-L195","doc":"Restricting a `∑ over univ` weighted by a membership indicator to a `∑ over S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.B2S","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.B2S","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L174-L178","doc":"**The doubled typed bond sum** of a proton-site set `S`. Doubled because each\nbond is counted from both ends, which keeps the statement inside a generic ring\nwith no division. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.deg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.deg","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L170-L172","doc":"The degree of a site, in the coefficient ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.emptyGraph","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.emptyGraph","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L162-L166","doc":"The edgeless graph, witnessing that `BondGraph` is inhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.irrefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.irrefl","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L160-L160","doc":"no self-bond ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.symm","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L158-L158","doc":"undirected ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.adj","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L156-L156","doc":"adjacency ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph.mk","kind":"ctor","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L154-L154","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.BondGraph","kind":"structure","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L151-L160","doc":"A finite simple graph on the sites, as a symmetric irreflexive boolean\nadjacency. (Data, not an assumption: every field is a structural fact about a\ngraph, and `BondGraph` is inhabited — see `emptyGraph`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.bondOf_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.bondOf_eq","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L141-L149","doc":"**The typed bond scalar is a quadratic polynomial in the two indicators.**\nThis is the step that makes the whole classification a `ring` computation: the\nthree-case definition is the *same function* as the bilinear form whose three\ncoefficients are `L_nn`, `L_pn − L_nn` and `L_pp − 2L_pn + L_nn`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.bondOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.bondOf","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L134-L139","doc":"The isospin-typed bond scalar: `true` is a proton. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.ind_false","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.ind_false","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.ind_true","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.ind_true","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L130-L130","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.ind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TypedBondSiteInvariance.ind","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TypedBondSiteInvariance.lean#L127-L128","doc":"The `{0,1}` indicator of a boolean, in the coefficient ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}